Relevant tables / columns and how they will be used  

• `open_images.annotations_bbox`  
  – `image_id`: joins to `open_images.images.image_id`  
  – `label_name`: filter for the cat synset ‘/m/01yrx’  
  – `confidence`: keep only rows with confidence = 1  

• `open_images.labels`  
  – Same three columns as above; can be inspected as an alternative human‑label source.  

• `open_images.images`  
  – `image_id`: primary key, used to join against the two label tables  
  – `original_url`: URL that we finally want to count (DISTINCT)  
  – `subset`: optional – lets you see which data split the image belongs to (train / val / test), but it is not strictly needed for the task.  



Ten exploratory → final queries
------------------------------------------------

```sql
-- 1. Description: Peek at 20 rows of annotations containing the cat label
SELECT *
FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_images.annotations_bbox`
WHERE label_name = '/m/01yrx'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Show 20 distinct image_ids that have the cat label (confidence = 1)
SELECT DISTINCT image_id
FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_images.annotations_bbox`
WHERE label_name = '/m/01yrx'
  AND confidence = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Join cat image_ids to the images table to see their URLs
SELECT i.image_id, i.original_url
FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_images.annotations_bbox` AS a
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.open_images.images`       AS i
  USING (image_id)
WHERE a.label_name = '/m/01yrx'
  AND a.confidence = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Count how many DISTINCT URLs belong to images that contain cats
SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT i.original_url) AS cat_url_cnt
FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_images.annotations_bbox` AS a
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.open_images.images`           AS i
  USING (image_id)
WHERE a.label_name = '/m/01yrx'
  AND a.confidence = 1;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Build a list of all image_ids that have the cat label (confidence = 1)
WITH cat_images AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT image_id
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_images.annotations_bbox`
  WHERE label_name = '/m/01yrx'
    AND confidence = 1
)
SELECT *
FROM cat_images
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Show 20 image URLs that do NOT contain cats
WITH cat_images AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT image_id
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_images.annotations_bbox`
  WHERE label_name = '/m/01yrx'
    AND confidence = 1
)
SELECT i.image_id, i.original_url
FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_images.images` AS i
LEFT JOIN cat_images           AS c
  ON i.image_id = c.image_id
WHERE c.image_id IS NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Count DISTINCT URLs of images that have NO cat label at all
WITH cat_images AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT image_id
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_images.annotations_bbox`
  WHERE label_name = '/m/01yrx'
    AND confidence = 1
)
SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT i.original_url) AS other_url_cnt
FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_images.images` AS i
LEFT JOIN cat_images AS c
  ON i.image_id = c.image_id
WHERE c.image_id IS NULL;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Produce both numbers (cat / other) side‑by‑side using UNION ALL
WITH cat_images AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT image_id
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_images.annotations_bbox`
  WHERE label_name = '/m/01yrx'
    AND confidence = 1
),
cat_urls AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT original_url
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_images.images` AS i
  JOIN cat_images                              AS c
  ON i.image_id = c.image_id
),
other_urls AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT original_url
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_images.images`
  WHERE image_id NOT IN (SELECT image_id FROM cat_images)
)
SELECT 'cat'   AS category, COUNT(*) AS url_cnt FROM cat_urls
UNION ALL
SELECT 'other' AS category, COUNT(*) AS url_cnt FROM other_urls;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Same as #8 but using COUNT IF for brevity
SELECT
  COUNT(DISTINCT IF(a.image_id IS NOT NULL, i.original_url, NULL)) AS cat_url_cnt,
  COUNT(DISTINCT IF(a.image_id IS NULL, i.original_url, NULL))     AS other_url_cnt
FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_images.images`           AS i
LEFT JOIN (
  SELECT DISTINCT image_id
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_images.annotations_bbox`
  WHERE label_name = '/m/01yrx'
    AND confidence = 1
) AS a
ON i.image_id = a.image_id;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: Alternative solution that uses the `labels` table
WITH cat_ids AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT image_id
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_images.labels`
  WHERE label_name = '/m/01yrx'
    AND confidence = 1
)
SELECT
  SUM(CASE WHEN i.image_id IN (SELECT * FROM cat_ids) THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS cat_images,
  SUM(CASE WHEN i.image_id NOT IN (SELECT * FROM cat_ids) THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS other_images
FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_images.images` AS i
LIMIT 20;
```

Execute either query #8 or #9 to obtain the final two counts:

• DISTINCT image URLs with a ‘cat’ (label = ‘/m/01yrx’, confidence = 1)  
• DISTINCT image URLs with no such label whatsoever (“other”)
